# FIXED DEFECT 2137, 2026-10-19, lane lane-witnessed-seed (panel 225's R1),
# the attack the critic ran on both prototypes (`forge2c`, `forge2p`,
# `forge3c`, `forge3p`): a header that writes the text of a probe's mark, as
# a line and through `_Pragma`, after a `pack` the guard resets.
#
# What it guards: the program's own unit reads `K_SZ` under `pack()` again,
# `sizeof` 8 and `INT_MIN / 2`, a value C defines; a copy cut at a mark the
# header wrote would read it under `pack(1)`, `sizeof` 5, and tell `K_SZ`
# undefined, false of this program. The marks are one identifier carrying
# the copy's own key, counted, so `narrow` is told alone.

extern "fixedbugs-2137-forged-marks.h"
    function narrow(x: i64) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type
    constant K_SZ: i64

function main()
    print(to_i64(narrow(x: 3)).must() + K_SZ)
